# UI redesign / CML feature migration

When work targets the **UI redesign branch** (FS ~1.10–based shell) or **reintroducing CML features** into that branch, follow the plan — do not paste old god-files for parity.

## Must read first

1. `docs/architecture/ui-redesign-migration.md` — order, definition of done, checklist, anti-patterns
2. `docs/architecture/code-organization.md` — orchestrator panels, shared dock, utils/passes
3. The area deep-dive under `docs/architecture/` for the feature touched

## Hard constraints

- **UI/architecture first**, then migrate features adapted to the new structure.
- Panels **orchestrate**; layout stays in the shared dock/layout system — no second splitter/tab engine.
- Keep CML strengths: event registration, addons, `BBSFeatures` gates, Actor Mode semantics.
- Do **not** drop CML product (toolbar, home/cross-world, etc.) silently — isolate as packages.
- Do **not** auto-port to other MC version branches unless the user explicitly asks.
- No gradle config edits; obey `CONTRIBUTING.md`.

## Quick reject

- Dumping `UIFilmPanel` / `UIReplaysEditor` / `ModelFormRenderer` monoliths unchanged
- Utils classes with no moved call sites
- Unfinished UI without a feature gate
